course: dictionary
lesson: 6903
title: The owner of a thing
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An owner is the person or group that something belongs to. If a bike is yours, you are its owner. Owner is a noun, so it names a person, and owners is more than one owner.
explain: Use the words around it to understand it. «A microchip is a tiny chip under a pet's skin that holds a number linked to the owner, so a lost pet can be returned.» The number leads back to the owner, so the lost pet can go home.
explain: Owner also helps with safety. «To stroke a dog, ask its owner first and let the dog sniff your hand.» The owner knows the dog, so ask before you touch it.
fact: An owner is a person or group that something belongs to.
fact: «Owners» means more than one owner.
fact: «Ask its owner first» means you should check with the person who owns the dog before you stroke it.
fact: If you find something, try to give it back to its owner.
fact: «The rightful owner» means the person who truly owns the thing.
exercise: «Herding dogs like sheepdogs may nip at running children's heels from instinct; the owner should call the dog off.» Who should call the dog off? | The dog's food bowl | The child who is running | *The owner | The neighbour's cat
exercise: Which word means the person that something belongs to? | finder | keeper | ownership | *owner
exercise: «A microchip is a tiny chip under a pet's skin that holds a number linked to the owner, so a lost pet can be returned.» Why is a microchip useful? | It makes the pet heavier | It keeps the pet warm | *It links a lost pet to its owner so it can go home | It tells the owner what the pet ate
test: In «the dog's owner», what does the 's show? | The dog is sad | It is a question mark | It means there are two dogs | *Whose owner it is: the owner belongs to the dog
test: Which word is the plural of owner? | ownership | owning | owner's | *owners
exam: «And Kieran swears rottweilers are killers, until he meets Maddie's neighbour's rottweiler, owner there, and it flops on its back for a belly rub.» Why should you ask the owner before stroking a dog? | Because owners are always cross | Because the dog cannot hear you | Because the owner has to give you a sweet | *Because the owner can tell you whether the dog is friendly
